{
  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5357",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to have a complex relationship with CAL-62 through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Mollicellin N to A704, which is targeted by palmarumycin CP18, and then to CAL-62. The second pathway connects Mollicellin N to P2X purinoceptor 1, which is targeted by a compound that also targets CAL-62. The third pathway links Mollicellin N to TE-9, which is targeted by the same compound as in the second pathway, again leading to CAL-62. These pathways suggest that Mollicellin N may act through different molecular mechanisms to ultimately influence CAL-62. The evidence supports a potential role for Mollicellin N in modulating CAL-62 through various receptor or signaling pathways, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
